%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: national level
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: Which national organization is the apex body for developing the
      National Curriculum Framework (NCF)?
    Options:
    - NCTE
    - UGC
    - NCERT
    - CBSE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The statutory body responsible for maintaining standards in teacher
      education and granting recognition to teacher education institutions is the:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - NCTE
    - NIEPA
    - CBSE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which national agency is primarily focused on the training of educational
      planners, administrators, and school principals?
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - NIOS
    - NCTE
    - NIEPA/NUEPA
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''NISHTHA'' program, a large-scale integrated teacher training
      initiative, is launched by the:'
    Options:
    - National Council for Teacher Education (NCTE)
    - Ministry of Education, Government of India
    - University Grants Commission (UGC)
    - Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which institution organizes Refresher Courses and Orientation Programs
      for college and university teachers through its Academic Staff Colleges?
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - AICTE
    - NCTE
    - UGC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The National Curriculum Framework for Teacher Education (NCFTE)
      is developed by the:'
    Options:
    - NCTE
    - NCERT
    - UGC
    - Ministry of Education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher from a CBSE-affiliated school would most likely attend
      subject-specific training organized by the:'
    Options:
    - State SCERT
    - Block Resource Centre
    - District DIET
    - Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The primary role of the NCERT in in-service teacher education
      is:'
    Options:
    - Administrative control over state governments
    - Research, development of training models, and capacity building of master trainers
    - Directly training every school teacher in India
    - Granting recognition to schools
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which national institution provides open and distance learning
      opportunities for in-service teachers to obtain qualifications like D.El.Ed.?
    Options:
    - NIOS
    - NCERT
    - UGC
    - IGNOU
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: The "PSS Central Institute of Vocational Education" is a constituent
      of which national body?
    Options:
    - NCTE
    - NCERT
    - UGC
    - NIOS
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which body's regulations ensure that an in-service diploma program
      for teachers meets minimum quality standards?
    Options:
    - CBSE
    - NCTE
    - NIEPA
    - ICSE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The national-level framework that guides the entire vision and
      content of teacher education in India is the:'
    Options:
    - National Education Policy (NEP)
    - National Curriculum Framework (NCF)
    - National Curriculum Framework for Teacher Education (NCFTE)
    - Right to Education Act (RTE)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The training of faculty from State Councils of Educational Research
      and Training (SCERTs) is primarily the responsibility of the:'
    Options:
    - DIETs
    - NCERT
    - State Government
    - Municipal Corporations
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a key function of the Ministry of Education
      in in-service teacher education?
    Options:
    - Developing detailed lesson plans for all subjects
    - Formulating national policy and launching flagship training schemes
    - Conducting classroom-level action research
    - Appointing teachers in state-government schools
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''C'' in the acronym CBSE stands for:'
    Options:
    - Central
    - Council
    - College
    - Commission
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'A workshop on "Leadership in School Education" for headteachers
      from across the country would most likely be organized by:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - NIEPA
    - NCTE
    - NIOS
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The development of the National Curriculum Framework (NCF) is
      a landmark function of the NCERT that influences in-service education because
      it:'
    Options:
    - Sets the syllabus for university exams
    - Designs school uniforms
    - Determines teacher salaries
    - Provides the philosophical and pedagogical basis for what and how teachers
      should teach
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which national body is specifically mandated for the quality assurance
      of higher education teachers' professional development?
    Options:
    - NCTE
    - UGC
    - AICTE
    - MCI
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''E'' in the acronym NIEPA stands for:'
    Options:
    - Economic
    - Educational
    - Elementary
    - Environmental
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The primary target group for the training programs of the University
      Grants Commission (UGC) is:'
    Options:
    - Elementary school teachers
    - Secondary school teachers
    - College and university teachers
    - School principals
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'A national-level workshop on implementing the recommendations
      of NEP 2020 in teacher education would be organized by the:'
    Options:
    - NCERT in collaboration with the Ministry of Education
    - State Directorate of Education
    - District Education Officer
    - Block Resource Centre
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''S'' in the acronym PSSCIVE stands for:'
    Options:
    - Science
    - Social
    - Sunderlal
    - Secondary
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which national institution provides a platform for online teacher
      training courses like the "Curriculum and School Leadership"?
    Options:
    - NIOS
    - CBSE
    - NCERT
    - NCTE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS) is crucial for
      in-service education as it:'
    Options:
    - Replaces all face-to-face training
    - Provides accessible professional development opportunities for teachers in
      remote areas
    - Focuses only on student examinations
    - Trains teachers for foreign countries
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''A'' in the acronym NIEPA stands for:'
    Options:
    - Administration
    - Association
    - Academy
    - Authority
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'A key function of the NCTE is to:'
    Options:
    - Publish textbooks for all classes
    - Lay down norms and standards for teacher education programs
    - Conduct board examinations for Class 10 and 12
    - Manage the finances of universities
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The national-level body that advises the central and state governments
      on policies and programs for qualitative improvement in school education is
      the:'
    Options:
    - UGC
    - NCERT
    - CBSE
    - AICTE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''R'' in the acronym NCERT stands for:'
    Options:
    - Reform
    - Rural
    - Regional
    - Research
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The "Capacity Building Programs" (CBPs) are a key in-service initiative
      of the:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - CBSE
    - NCTE
    - NIOS
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ultimate goal of all national-level agencies in in-service
      teacher education is to:'
    Options:
    - Increase the number of government employees
    - Standardize teaching methods across India
    - Improve the overall quality of education by enhancing teacher competence
    - Reduce the cost of education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which national body would be involved in the development of a model
      ICT curriculum for teachers?
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology
    - ISRO
    - Department of Science and Technology
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''T'' in the acronym NCTE stands for:'
    Options:
    - Teaching
    - Training
    - Technology
    - Tertiary
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'A college lecturer attending a Refresher Course in "Environmental
      Science" is participating in a program mandated by the:'
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - AICTE
    - NCTE
    - UGC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The national-level framework that influences the design of all
      in-service teacher education programs is the:'
    Options:
    - National Policy on Education (NPE)
    - National Curriculum Framework for Teacher Education (NCFTE)
    - Five-Year Plan
    - National Skill Development Mission
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The "I" in the acronym NIOS stands for:'
    Options:
    - Indian
    - International
    - Institute
    - Integrated
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which national agency is responsible for the "Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan"
      (SSA) and "Samagra Shiksha" schemes, which have a significant in-service training
      component?
    Options:
    - NCERT
    - Ministry of Education
    - NCTE
    - NIEPA
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'A key contribution of NCERT to in-service education is the development
      of:'
    Options:
    - Teacher recruitment policies for states
    - Innovative teaching-learning materials and modules
    - School building designs
    - Teacher salary structures
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''P'' in the acronym PSSCIVE stands for:'
    Options:
    - Primary
    - Professional
    - Public
    - Pandit
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The national-level structure for in-service teacher education
      ensures:'
    Options:
    - Complete autonomy for each school
    - A common vision and standard of quality across the country
    - That training is only theoretical
    - The elimination of state-level agencies
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which national body focuses exclusively on the professional development
      of teachers and heads of vocational streams?
    Options:
    - NCTE
    - PSSCIVE
    - UGC
    - AICTE
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The "National Mission on Teachers and Teaching" is an initiative
      of the:'
    Options:
    - Ministry of Education
    - Ministry of Health
    - Ministry of Defence
    - Ministry of Agriculture
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''O'' in the acronym NIOS stands for:'
    Options:
    - Organization
    - Open
    - Official
    - Operational
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'A major challenge for national-level agencies is:'
    Options:
    - Lack of any policies to implement
    - Ensuring the effective trickle-down of training and resources to the grassroots
      level
    - The absence of a regulatory framework
    - Having no state-level partners
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The relationship between NCERT and SCERT is best described as:'
    Options:
    - A competitive one
    - A hierarchical one where SCERT directs NCERT
    - A collaborative one where NCERT provides the framework and SCERT adapts it
    - Non-existent
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The ''V'' in the acronym PSSCIVE stands for:'
    Options:
    - Value
    - Virtual
    - Village
    - Vocational
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: Which national body's guidelines ensure that an in-service certificate
      course for elementary teachers has a minimum duration and credit structure?
    Options:
    - CBSE
    - NCTE
    - NCERT
    - UGC
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The "Centres of Excellence" for teacher training are established
      by the:'
    Options:
    - NIOS
    - CBSE
    - State Governments
    - Municipalities
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The development of the "Learning Outcomes" document for each class
      and subject was initiated by the:'
    Options:
    - NCTE
    - NIOS
    - UGC
    - NCERT
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: national level
  - QuestionText: 'The comprehensive approach of national-level agencies ensures
      that in-service teacher education is viewed as a:'
    Options:
    - One-time requirement for promotion
    - Systematic and continuous component of a teacher's career
    - Responsibility solely of the teacher
    - Luxury for a few selected teachers
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: national level
